The objective was to automate grade validation for a student dataset.

Input Processing: The script reads marks.txt using a comma as the Internal Field Separator (IFS=',').

Conditional Logic: It checks three subject variables (m1, m2, m3) against a threshold of 33.

Counting: For each student, it counts the number of failures. If a student fails exactly one subject, the fail_one counter is incremented; if they fail none, the pass_all counter is incremented.

Final Report: After reading the entire file, the script prints the total summary of students who passed all or failed exactly one.
